# Canonical Stack Defaults

Unless the repository already mandates a different stack, use these defaults for new work:

## Python backend / services
- Python 3.12+
- uv for dependency and environment management
- FastAPI for HTTP APIs when an API framework is needed
- Pydantic v2 for schemas and settings
- SQLAlchemy 2.x + Alembic for relational persistence
- pytest for tests
- Ruff for linting/formatting where the repo uses Ruff
- mypy or pyright if the repo already uses static typing checks

## Frontend / web apps
- Next.js App Router
- TypeScript
- pnpm
- src/ directory layout
- import alias `@/*`
- Tailwind CSS when the repo uses Tailwind
- one repo-approved linter/formatter strategy
- feature-oriented component structure

## Monorepo conventions
- pnpm workspace for JS/TS packages
- clear package boundaries
- shared libraries only when they represent real reuse
- no duplicate app-local utility copies when a stable shared package already exists

## General engineering standards
- environment-driven configuration
- no hardcoded secrets
- strong typing
- contract-first interfaces
- tests required for meaningful behavior changes
- additive, migration-safe changes by default